    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d604">

                <pb facs="0681" n="663" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg663"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20210/5–1046: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-10T13:00:00-05:00">May 10, 1946—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:23 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>328. ReDepcirtel April 30,<anchor n="36"
                        xml:id="d604-f1"/> dissolution German institutions, schools and other means
                    propaganda appears complete in entire country. No German schools, cultural
                    institutions or other propaganda agencies are functioning in Republic today.
                    Only one German school operated as such in Bogotá until US entry in war. That
                    school collapsed beginning of war. Same thing happened with Colegio Alemán
                    Transocean and Nazi Party in Medellin and other districts. No renewed German
                    activity of any kind noted in Colombia to date.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
